From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:06:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Widen the entity slice bucket columns to four blocks as well

0214 coarsened the Z rows to four blocks because a one-block cell was crossed almost
every tick and the maintenance ate the whole query gain. The X columns were left at one
block, which is what they had been since the index was introduced - but the same
argument applies to them, and it turns out they were past the same optimum.

Four-block columns as well, so a bucket is (x << 2) | z over sixteen cells. Verified
with debugVerifyAthenaIndexes against the flat slice walk - 6,905,955 bucketed entity
checks, no mismatch.

Measured +1.62% TPS, 6/6 pairwise wins, on top of 0214 at 30,000 golems with four bots.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Chunk.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Chunk.java
index 3864d805db2b8e1725c2fd002953c88fb79baa41..3d67d0a90ff8879a33bd011c6da83fffc49998e8 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Chunk.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Chunk.java
@@ -786,10 +786,10 @@ public class Chunk {
     }
 
     // Athena start - bucket index maintenance
-    /** The bucket column a world X coordinate falls in, clamped to this chunk. */
+    /** The bucket column a world X coordinate falls in, clamped to this chunk. Four blocks wide. */
     private int bucketOf(double x) {
-        int b = MathHelper.floor(x) - (this.locX << 4);
-        return b < 0 ? 0 : (b > 15 ? 15 : b);
+        int b = (MathHelper.floor(x) - (this.locX << 4)) >> 2;
+        return b < 0 ? 0 : (b > 3 ? 3 : b);
     }
 
     /** The bucket row a world Z coordinate falls in, clamped to this chunk. Four blocks deep. */
@@ -832,7 +832,7 @@ public class Chunk {
 
     /** Builds (or rebuilds) the bucket index of one slice from the slice itself. */
     private void buildBuckets(int slice) {
-        List<Entity>[] buckets = (List<Entity>[]) new List[64]; // Athena - 16 x 4
+        List<Entity>[] buckets = (List<Entity>[]) new List[16]; // Athena - 4 x 4
 
         this.entityBuckets[slice] = buckets;
         this.bucketPadX[slice] = 1;
